  "title": "Battle of Tondibi",
  "summary": "In March 1591 a Moroccan army under Djudar Pasha defeated the Songhai army of Askia Ishak II at Tondibi, about 56 km from Gao. Moroccan firearms outgunned Songhai spears and bows. Djudar seized the deserted Gao, and Morocco took Timbuktu and Djenné; the defeat is regarded as the end of the Songhai Empire.",
